<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fresh loins were mostly $4.00 higher; butts $2.00-5.00 higher; skinned hams 17-20 lbs steady to $2.00 higher, 20-26 lbs $1.00-3.00 higher; seedless bellies $2.00-3.00 higher; lean trimmings $4.00-7.00 higher.-USDA</p>
<p>Trade was slow, with moderate to good demand and light offerings.</p>
<p>NOTE: 0.5 ld. of 14-18 lb. loins traded at $112.00.</p>
